WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.812
InfinityGAN asks a bold question: can a model
synthesize images of arbitrary,

00:00:05.892 --> 00:00:11.553
even infinite size, while training only on small
patches on a single consumer GPU?

00:00:11.633 --> 00:00:15.684
Existing high-resolution GANs fail because compute,
memory,

00:00:15.764 --> 00:00:18.625
and data all scale with output resolution.

00:00:18.705 --> 00:00:24.227
InfinityGAN breaks that coupling, disentangling an
image into global appearance,

00:00:24.307 --> 00:00:26.608
local structure, and fine texture,

00:00:26.688 --> 00:00:32.139
and generating any region patch-by-patch from
continuous coordinates, seamless,

00:00:32.219 --> 00:00:35.150
globally consistent, and unbounded in size.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:39.332
Modern generative models keep improving in
resolution and detail,

00:00:39.412 --> 00:00:43.215
but every gain costs more training time, a bigger model,

00:00:43.295 --> 00:00:47.097
and large field-of-view images that are hard to collect.

00:00:47.177 --> 00:00:50.980
Worse, existing generators are locked to their
training resolution.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:54.862
Push them larger,

00:00:54.942 --> 00:00:58.745
and compute and memory explode quadratically while
global structure falls apart.

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:02.627
InfinityGAN asks how to escape this coupling and
synthesize arbitrary,

00:01:02.707 --> 00:01:06.510
even infinite images from finite data on modest hardware.

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:10.021
Why do existing models fail when asked to grow?

00:01:10.101 --> 00:01:17.057
The insight: generators like StyleGAN2 secretly
rely on zero-padding at the borders to encode position.

00:01:17.137 --> 00:01:22.112
During training the padding pattern is fixed, so
the network memorizes it.

00:01:22.192 --> 00:01:26.211
But synthesize a larger image, and the feature size
changes,

00:01:26.291 --> 00:01:28.670
the padding-derived position shifts,

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:33.315
and the image center no longer gets sensible
positional information,

00:01:33.395 --> 00:01:35.842
producing repetitive, broken content.

00:01:35.922 --> 00:01:41.102
Truly infinite synthesis needs position valid
infinitely far from any border,

00:01:41.182 --> 00:01:43.630
plus patches that combine seamlessly.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:48.185
InfinityGAN makes five contributions.

00:01:48.265 --> 00:01:52.440
First, it reframes generation as disentangling
global appearance, local structure,

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:56.695
and fine texture, each with a dedicated component.

00:01:56.775 --> 00:02:00.950
Second,

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:05.205
a structure synthesizer built as a neural implicit
function driven by continuous coordinates,

00:02:05.285 --> 00:02:09.460
so any sub-region can be queried directly.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:13.715
Third, a padding-free generator removing all zero-padding,

00:02:13.795 --> 00:02:17.970
letting patches synthesize independently yet
combine seamlessly.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:22.225
Fourth, a scale-invariant FID metric for sizes
where no real reference images exist.

00:02:22.305 --> 00:02:26.480
Finally, applications the design unlocks, from
spatial style fusion to outpainting.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:29.459
InfinityGAN's generator has two modules.

00:02:29.539 --> 00:02:36.357
The structure synthesizer is a neural implicit
function: it takes a global latent for scene appearance,

00:02:36.437 --> 00:02:41.045
a local latent tensor for variation, and a
continuous coordinate grid,

00:02:41.125 --> 00:02:44.192
and outputs a structural latent for any region.

00:02:44.272 --> 00:02:50.085
Coordinates use sine-cosine horizontally to exploit
landscape self-similarity and a tanh

00:02:50.165 --> 00:02:52.898
vertically for the ground-to-sky gradient,

00:02:52.978 --> 00:02:56.381
so it can be queried infinitely far from the origin.

00:02:56.461 --> 00:03:02.341
The texture synthesizer is a fully-convolutional
StyleGAN2 with all zero-padding removed,

00:03:02.421 --> 00:03:06.895
turning the structural latent, global style, and
noise into a patch.

00:03:06.975 --> 00:03:11.449
With no padding, the same coordinate always yields
identical pixels,

00:03:11.529 --> 00:03:15.333
so independent patches tile seamlessly at constant memory.

00:03:15.413 --> 00:03:19.217
Training combines adversarial, R1, path-length, diversity,

00:03:19.297 --> 00:03:22.030
and vertical-coordinate regression losses.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:25.129
The authors introduce Flickr-Landscape,

00:03:25.209 --> 00:03:30.728
four hundred fifty thousand high-quality landscape
images crawled from Flickr,

00:03:30.808 --> 00:03:33.599
to evaluate synthesis at extended sizes.

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:37.475
For outpainting they use scenery subsets of Places365,

00:03:37.555 --> 00:03:41.710
sixty-two thousand five hundred images, and
Flickr-Scenery,

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:43.576
about fifty-four thousand.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:49.390
Remarkably, every InfinityGAN model trains on tiny
one-hundred-one-pixel patches,

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:54.630
and both training and any-size inference run on a
single GTX TITAN X GPU.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:57.268
On the Flickr-Landscape benchmark,

00:03:57.348 --> 00:04:01.189
InfinityGAN holds a steady quality slope as output grows,

00:04:01.269 --> 00:04:04.696
while baselines drift far from realistic structure.

00:04:04.776 --> 00:04:08.823
Beyond four-times extension it beats the strongest
baseline,

00:04:08.903 --> 00:04:16.664
scoring a scale-invariant FID of sixty-one point
four at four-times versus seventy-nine point eight for StyleGAN2,

00:04:16.744 --> 00:04:20.584
and one twenty-one versus one eighty-nine at eight-times.

00:04:20.664 --> 00:04:26.017
Its memory stays constant, while StyleGAN2 runs out
of memory at sixteen-times.

00:04:26.097 --> 00:04:29.800
And over ninety percent preferred it over every method.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:34.702
The central ablation isolates where positional
information comes from.

00:04:34.782 --> 00:04:37.858
Starting from StyleGAN2 with non-constant input,

00:04:37.938 --> 00:04:40.422
the authors strip out all zero-padding,

00:04:40.502 --> 00:04:44.104
creating a padding-free variant with no positional cues.

00:04:44.184 --> 00:04:49.890
It fails to generate reasonable structure and
degrades sharply across every FID setting,

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:54.755
confirming the original generator leaned entirely
on padding for position.

00:04:54.835 --> 00:04:57.056
Add the structure synthesizer back,

00:04:57.136 --> 00:05:02.119
and position is now supplied through the
coordinate-driven structural latent,

00:05:02.199 --> 00:05:04.880
so quality returns, validating the design.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:12.159
The headline numbers: scale-invariant FID of
sixty-one at four-times and one twenty-one at eight-times,

00:05:12.239 --> 00:05:14.598
both beating the strongest baseline.

00:05:14.678 --> 00:05:17.105
Over ninety percent human preference.

00:05:17.185 --> 00:05:21.916
Up to seven point two times faster inference
through parallel batching,

00:05:21.996 --> 00:05:27.946
cutting eight-thousand-pixel synthesis from one
hundred thirty-seven seconds to nineteen.

00:05:28.026 --> 00:05:30.588
Paired with In-and-Out for outpainting,

00:05:30.668 --> 00:05:36.280
FID drops to nine on Places365 and fifteen on
Flickr-Scenery, halving previous best.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:43.915
The takeaway: infinite-pixel synthesis becomes
tractable once you stop tying generation to a fixed resolution.

00:05:43.995 --> 00:05:46.049
By separating global appearance,

00:05:46.129 --> 00:05:49.917
local structure via a coordinate-driven implicit function,

00:05:49.997 --> 00:05:52.651
and texture via a padding-free generator,

00:05:52.731 --> 00:05:57.653
InfinityGAN produces patches that are independent
yet perfectly consistent,

00:05:57.733 --> 00:06:02.721
tiling into images of any size at constant memory
and generated in parallel.

00:06:02.801 --> 00:06:07.589
The same framework unlocks spatial style fusion,
multi-modal outpainting,

00:06:07.669 --> 00:06:11.190
and arbitrary-length panoramas, all from tiny patches.
